# demand_diff_pub_1 -- oracle input batches: the demand-blind add_edge stream
# (adds + net-removals mirroring the driver's d1/d2 in-answer edge retracts).
# The oracle evaluates the plain UNDEMANDED program and NETS the retractions to
# the surviving rows; the demand probes (query surface) are absent here.
# nbhd_out = the NET single-hop of add_edge.
#
# e1: add_edge adds.
batch
+ add_edge 1 10
+ add_edge 1 20
+ add_edge 3 30
end
# d1: retract in-answer edge (1,10) under standing demand.
batch
- add_edge 1 10
end
# d2: retract in-answer edge (3,30) under standing demand.
batch
- add_edge 3 30
end
